#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:5
#: c9fb1664a11444acb1930a4557ffc62d
msgid "GPS Failsafe and Glitch Protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:7
#: 070b5a058a424e8c810b1b8883e0ce4f
msgid "This article describes the glitch protection mechanisms used to trigger GPS Failsafe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:11
#: 844590b8bac54953bddc509bdd962e42
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:13
#: 49559b53038c4b52aa4d362c14b04b9d
msgid "GPS Systems can occasionally drop the signal or provide significantly inaccurate position information (aka \"glitches\"). While errors are more likely in conditions where the GPS signal can bounce off multiple paths before reaching the receiver (multipathing), errors can occasionally occur even with clear sky."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:19
#: 858af50731964261a4b4a5529f42c24a
msgid "A *GPS failsafe* event will occur if GPS 3D lock or the position \"Glitches\" for at least 5 seconds while Copter is in a mode that requires the GPS (RTL, Auto, Loiter, Circle, Position, Guided or Drift).  The GPS failsafe response can be set to Land or switch to AltHold mode so that you can retake manual control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:26
#: a069f3a3152741b1b346eceb582ca3bd
msgid "Without GPS updates, the inertial sensors allow approximately 10 seconds of accurate position information but after this the horizontal position drift becomes so large that the horizontal position cannot be maintained at all.  At this point if you still have RC radio control it is recommended to take back control using Stabilize, Acro or AltHold as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:34
#: 1afcc27fb90f4d59a7830f1873a3c845
msgid "Glitch Protection - Default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:36
#: d87fae77a4424c66b22cad20c1c5e727
msgid "GPS glitch protection is provided which can help alert the pilot to a bad GPS position, trigger a failsafe and reduce the incidents of fly-aways.  Glitches are detected by comparing the each new position update received from the GPS with a position projected out from the previous update's position and velocity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:45
#: 4ca952c74e0f45c69bf1ba94618a901e
msgid "The new position is accepted as \"good\" if:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:47
#: 2c3d13aed9314dd3b3351d2653df3cab
msgid "the two positions are within the ``GPSGLITCH_RADIUS`` (defaults to 5m)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:49
#: 6a80dbcb7273475d865d971124a6d4b0
msgid "the new position is within a radius that is 10m/s/s (``GPSGLITCH_ACCEL``) \\* dt \\* dt.  Where \"dt\" is the time difference between the two samples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:53
#: 517ce30d24e4455abef16270b79ad96b
msgid "During a glitch, \"Bad Position\" will be written on the ground station's HUD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:57
#: 5b14715ed76d4fbd85af6db7ab3b4155
msgid "Glitch Protection - EKF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:59
#: f4f1610f33ad47e79e5abdf0bf665da0
msgid ":ref:`ArduPilot Extended Kalman Filter (EKF) <common-apm-navigation-extended-kalman-filter-overview>`)provided glitch protection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:62
#: 9a1e69c8a7864fddb52c7220e084b6d7
msgid "Glitch protection using the EKF works as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:64
#: 131a550cf48545fbbb1eb330eae2a2cc
msgid "When new GPS position measurements are received, they are compared to a position predicted using IMU measurements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:66
#: 2ab6a2ea3a1b45379929900854bb5081
msgid "If the difference exceeds a statistical confidence level set by ``EKF_POS_GATE``, then the measurement won't be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:68
#: c7860159e02f4859ac2080683e65be74
msgid "While GPS measurements aren't being used, a circle defined by an uncertainty radius grows around the predicted position. The rate at which this radius grows is controlled by ``EKF_GLITCH_ACCEL``. This is similar to the circle defined by ``GPSGLITCH_ACCEL``, the difference being it is centered around the trajectory predicted by the IMU rather than previous GPS measurements. Because this allows for deviations in trajectory due to maneuvers, the default value for ``EKF_GLTCH_ACCEL`` is smaller at 1.5 m/s/s. The acceleration growth of the circle is also increased when the vehicle is accelerating or turning to allow for the increase in IMU errors during maneuvers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:78
#: 640655d963704f69820c964f13d2631a
msgid "If subsequent GPS measurements fall inside the circle, they will be accepted and the circle is reset back to the minimum radius controlled by ``EKF_POS_GATE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gps-failsafe-glitch-protection.rst:81
#: bac03ad253d246e58f944aad32f6d5b0
msgid "If the GPS glitch is large enough and lasts long enough, the GPS measurements will continue to be rejected until the circle radius exceeds a value set by ``EKF_GLITCH_RAD``. When this happens, an offset is applied to the GPS position so that it matches the estimated vehicle position and the GPS positions are used again. The GPS offset is then reduced to zero at 1 m/s. This means that large long duration glitches will cause the vehicle to drift at a 1 m/s rate. This is slow enough to give the operator plenty of time to react."
msgstr ""
